<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan forex reserves slip to $1.502 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan forex reserves slip to $1.502 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves fell to $1.502 billion as of May 24 from $1.569 billion on May 17, the State Bank of Pakistan said on Thursday.</p>
<p>That compares with foreign exchange reserves of $2.136 billion a year ago, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The following is the weekly foreign exchange reserves holdings position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (BLN DLRS)	   MAY 24   MAY 17    MAY 23, 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL			 1.502    1.569     2.136</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan	 0.569    0.617     1.328</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan  0.260    0.276     0.110</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion  0.671    0.673     0.696</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights  0.001    0.003     0.001</p>
<p>((-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192))</p>
